---
// DRAFT privacy policy — review (ideally with legal counsel) before relying on it.
// Content reflects exactly what the Megabait analytics system collects as of the
// effective date below. Update the effective date and controller details as needed.
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const effectiveDate = 'August 17, 2026';
---

<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<meta charset="utf-8" />
		<link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="32x32" href="/favicon-32.png" />
		<link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="48x48" href="/favicon-48.png" />
		<link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/apple-touch-icon.png" />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
		<meta name="generator" content={Astro.generator} />
		<meta name="description" content="Privacy policy for Megabait and RebotGames — what optional gameplay data we collect, why, and how to control it." />
		<title>Privacy Policy — RebotGames</title>
	</head>
	<body>
		<main class="policy">
			<p class="back"><a href="/">&larr; RebotGames</a></p>

			<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
			<p class="effective">Effective {effectiveDate}</p>

			<p>
				This policy explains the optional gameplay data our game <strong>Megabait</strong>
				collects, why we collect it, and the choices you have. We keep data collection
				minimal and only use it to make the game better.
			</p>

			<h2>Who we are</h2>
			<p>
				Megabait is developed by <strong>RebotGames</strong> ("we", "us"), the data
				controller for the data described here. You can reach us at
				<a href="mailto:hello@rebotgames.com">hello@rebotgames.com</a> for any privacy
				question or request.
			</p>

			<h2>Analytics are optional and off by default</h2>
			<p>
				When you first launch Megabait, we ask whether you want to share gameplay
				analytics. <strong>Nothing is collected unless you choose "Allow."</strong> You
				can change your mind at any time from the in-game <em>Settings</em> menu, and no
				data is collected while running the game from the development editor.
			</p>

			<h2>What we collect (only if you allow it)</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>Your <strong>Steam ID</strong> as a player identifier when you play through
					Steam. This lets us group your sessions together.</li>
				<li>Your <strong>country</strong>, at 2-letter level only (for example "ES" or
					"US"). Steam derives this from your IP address and gives us only the country
					code. <strong>We never receive or store your IP address</strong>, and we do
					not collect your region or city.</li>
				<li>Basic technical context: <strong>platform</strong> (Windows, Linux, or
					macOS) and the <strong>game version</strong> you are playing.</li>
				<li><strong>Gameplay events</strong>: which levels you start and finish, how many
					attempts and how long they take, and the in-level positions where your
					character dies together with the hazard that caused it.</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>Why we collect it</h2>
			<p>
				Solely to improve the game. Balancing difficulty, finding levels or hazards that
				are unfair or frustrating, and understanding where our players are. We do
				<strong>not</strong> use this data for advertising or profiling, and we do not
				sell or share it.
			</p>
			<p>
				Our legal basis under the GDPR is your <strong>consent</strong>, which you give
				through the first-run prompt and can withdraw at any time inside the in-game settings. Withdrawing
				consent stops any further collection.
			</p>

			<h2>What we do not collect</h2>
			<p>
				We do not collect your name, email address, payment details, or any "special
				category" data (such as data revealing health, ethnicity, religion, or political
				views). Purchases are handled entirely by Steam; we never see your payment
				information.
			</p>

			<h2>Where your data is stored</h2>
			<p>
				Analytics data is stored using <strong>Supabase</strong>, our database provider,
				which processes it on our behalf. Your Steam ID and gameplay come to us through
				<strong>Valve's Steam</strong> platform, whose own
				<a href="https://store.steampowered.com/privacy_agreement/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">privacy policy</a>
				governs your use of Steam itself.
			</p>

			<h2>How long we keep it</h2>
			<p>
				We keep analytics data only as long as it is useful for improving the game and
				remove old data periodically. You can also ask us to delete your data at any time
				(see below).
			</p>

			<h2>Your rights</h2>
			<p>
				You can withdraw consent at any time by turning analytics off in the in-game
				Settings menu. You may also ask us to give you a copy of, or to delete, the data
				associated with your player identifier by emailing
				<a href="mailto:hello@rebotgames.com">hello@rebotgames.com</a>. Depending on where
				you live, you may have additional rights under laws such as the GDPR, including
				the right to lodge a complaint with your local data protection authority.
			</p>

			<h2>Children</h2>
			<p>
				Megabait is not directed at children, and we do not knowingly collect data from
				children. If you believe a child has provided us data, contact us and we will
				delete it.
			</p>

			<h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
			<p>
				We may update this policy as the game evolves. Material changes will be reflected
				here with an updated effective date.
			</p>

			<h2>Contact</h2>
			<p>
				Questions or requests: <a href="mailto:hello@rebotgames.com">hello@rebotgames.com</a>.
			</p>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style is:global>
	:root {
		--color-bg: #0b1014;
		--color-fg: #f1f5f9;
		--color-muted: #94a3b8;
		--color-border: #1f2933;
		--color-accent: #7fffd4;
	}

	* {
		box-sizing: border-box;
	}

	html,
	body {
		margin: 0;
		padding: 0;
	}

	body {
		background: var(--color-bg);
		color: var(--color-fg);
		font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif;
	}

	a {
		color: var(--color-accent);
		text-decoration: none;
	}

	a:hover {
		text-decoration: underline;
	}
</style>

<style>
	.policy {
		max-width: 46rem;
		margin: 0 auto;
		padding: 3rem 1.5rem 1rem;
		line-height: 1.65;
	}

	.back a {
		color: var(--color-muted);
		font-size: 0.9rem;
	}

	h1 {
		margin: 1rem 0 0.25rem;
		font-size: 2rem;
	}

	.effective {
		color: var(--color-muted);
		font-size: 0.9rem;
		margin-top: 0;
	}

	h2 {
		margin-top: 2.25rem;
		font-size: 1.2rem;
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
		padding-bottom: 0.35rem;
	}

	ul {
		padding-left: 1.25rem;
	}

	li {
		margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
	}
</style>
